You are working in a React Native project using Expo (managed workflow).

Assume:
- Expo SDK APIs are preferred over custom native code
- Cross-platform compatibility (iOS + Android) is required
- The app runs in Android Emulator and iOS Simulator, not a physical device
- Modern React with hooks and functional components only

When generating code:
- Use React Native components, not HTML elements
- Avoid browser-specific APIs (window, document, localStorage)
- Avoid Node.js-only APIs (fs, path, process)
- Prefer Expo libraries (expo-av, expo-image, expo-haptics, expo-router)
- Use StyleSheet or inline styles, not CSS
- Use Flexbox for layout

Navigation:
- Prefer expo-router unless explicitly told otherwise
- Use file-based routing conventions correctly
- Redirects in useEffect: use the useRedirectOnce hook (hooks/useRedirectOnce.ts) so the redirect runs at most once. Never redirect based on auth/session in an effect without this guard, or you risk infinite redirect loops between index and layout.

State & data:
- Prefer React hooks and lightweight state (useState, useEffect)
- Avoid Redux unless explicitly requested
- Assume async storage uses expo-secure-store or @react-native-async-storage

Performance & UX:
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Use FlatList instead of ScrollView for long lists
- Respect mobile gestures and safe areas

Debugging:
- Prefer console.log and Expo DevTools-compatible debugging
- Avoid instructions requiring physical devices unless requested

Output:
- Provide complete, runnable code examples
- Do not include web-specific setup steps unless explicitly requested
